No, you're not the only one. I agree.

So, I don't play spork, I have my own preferred choice of patches that I
use. Ones that don't change the plot. My philosophy with patches is that I
want to keep my games comparable to unpatched vanilla Nethack.
So I generally don't use patches that add or remove items, monsters or
dungeon features or change the behavior of existing ones. I mainly have
just interface patches that show more information when the game is over or
make it easier to see some information that is already given to the player
but doesn't stand out as clearly as I'd like, or make something easier to
do. (The dump and extinct/showborn patches are examples of more
information after the game, hpmon and menucolor about showing something
more clearly and sortloot about an easier way to do something.)

I realize that some people like bigger changes, but like I said, I prefer
keeping my version essentially close to vanilla and the changes done in a
way that they can be turned off by runtime options whenever practically
possible. 

